  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Facilities-Planning-and-Management/Facility-Maintainer-III_JR100031": {
      "title": "Facility Maintainer III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCustodial Services ‌ Job Summary: Drake University's Office of Facilities Planning & Management performs a variety of custodial tasks and activities designed to maintain the campus in an orderly, sanitary, safe and attractive condition. The Facility Maintainer III (FMIII) works under general supervision, with daily periods of self-directed activity to complete work activities that are scheduled, unscheduled, and are subject to frequent interruptions. Under supervision, but with regular daily periods of self directed activity, performs a variety of tasks and activities designed to maintain the University in an orderly sanitary, safe and attractive condition. Work activities are scheduled and unscheduled in nature and are subject to frequent interruptions. Work schedule is mornings, Saturday and Sunday 5am to 1:30pm and 3 weekday's from 4:30am to 1:00pm. Position requires a pre-employment background check, drug screen, and a valid driver's license and a driving record that meets the insurability requirements to drive on behalf of the University. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED Limited: 0-1 year Valid Iowa Driver's License, good driving record and insurable by Drake Preferred Qualifications: Ability to read and communicate in writing using the English language Housekeeping experience preferred Ability to satisfactorily complete department training program Ability to follow instructions Ability to consistently meet the department work schedule as designated Ability to work with chemical fluids used for cleaning, waxing and/or disinfecting Ability to lift 50lbs Ability to wear a backpack vacuum. Must be able to follow safety protocols Essential Job Functions: 30% Vacuums, dust mops, damp and wet mop stairwells, restrooms, hallways, classrooms and offices 30% Cleans and disinfects areas by washing with germicidal cleaning solutions, polish sinks, drinking fountains, toilets, mirrors and similar apparatus; spot wash walls, light switches and telephones; wash or clean windows and door glass; keep all debris in area picked up. 20% Utilizes chemical supplies and equipment to complete tasks, including exercising judgment to choose appropriate chemical and equipment for each task. 15% Collects and removes waste inside and outside of University buildings 5%other duties as assigned ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email tammy.eltayb@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check and drug screen. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Drake-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Teaching-and-Learning_JR100030": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Teaching and Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nSchool of Education JM ‌ Department Summary: At Drake University's School of Education, we prepare world-class teachers and educational leaders. With more than 1,000 undergraduate and graduate students, we’re one of the largest schools of education in the Midwest—and for good reason. We have an exceptional record of preparing highly effective elementary and secondary teachers, school counselors, principals, superintendents, and specialists working in training and organizational development in the corporate and non-profit sectors. At the same time, we don’t let our size compromise our commitment to providing an intimate learning environment that fosters close connections between students and faculty. Drake University’s School of Education consists of dedicated, high-energy educators of future educators. We are dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning. We seek faculty who will truly care about the student experience and take pride in their work. Our dedication is demonstrated through ongoing support for faculty in developing their teaching craft through access to numerous, resourced professional development opportunities. Job Summary: The Drake University Teaching and Learning Department invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor. This position will be responsible for teaching a three-credit graduate section of specific Montessori content area courses as part of the MSE: Montessori Education degree program. The successful candidate will teach one section in the spring of 2027. The course outcomes have already been developed in connection with MACTE accreditation. Two instructors will be hired. Minimum Qualifications: A master’s degree Montessori certification in both Elementary Levels I and II 3 years of teaching in a Montessori classroom are required ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email jill.johnson@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Drake-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Accounting_JR100029": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nZimpleman College of Business JM ‌ Department Summary: Drake University's Zimpleman College of Business is committed to nurturing a high-performance work culture that provides meaningful career opportunities for faculty and staff, and is focused on creating an authentically diverse, inclusive, and equitable environment for all. The College's North Star is centered on equipping students to do well by doing good, empowering them to contribute to the global economy and society. With 54 full-time faculty and staff members, we work as a team to ensure Zimpleman students are equipped with the technical skills, business acumen, and experience to prepare them for immediate and lasting success. To learn more about the College, visit: https://www.drake.edu/zimpleman/ Job Summary: Essential duties include teaching two undergraduate introductory managerial accounting courses during the spring semester, 2027. Course topics include, but are not limited to, managerial accounting foundations, job order costing, process costing, activity based costing, cost-volume-profit analysis, incremental analysis, pricing, budgeting, and standard costs. As part of the teaching duties, the candidate is expected to evaluate student performance and assign grades, as well as meet periodically with a supervisor to discuss teaching performance. Minimum Qualifications: A graduate degree in accounting or closely related field and/or possess significant experience directly related to the field of accounting Preferred Qualifications: • Evidence of demonstrated effectiveness (student course evaluations) in teaching at the university level • significant accounting experience • accounting related professional certification ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.  If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email sheri.gavin@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Drake-University/Adjunct--Information-Systems_JR100028": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Information Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nZimpleman College of Business JM ‌ Department Summary: Drake University's Zimpleman College of Business is committed to nurturing a high-performance work culture that provides meaningful career opportunities for faculty and staff, and is focused on creating an authentically diverse, inclusive, and equitable environment for all. The College's North Star is centered on equipping students to do well by doing good, empowering them to contribute to the global economy and society. With 54 full-time faculty and staff members, we work as a team to ensure Zimpleman students are equipped with the technical skills, business acumen, and experience to prepare them for immediate and lasting success. To learn more about the College, visit: https://www.drake.edu/zimpleman/ Job Summary: Drake University's Zimpleman College of Business invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor in Information Systems to teach Information Systems Analysis and Design for Spring, 2027. The focus of the course is to provide an introduction to strategies and technologies for analyzing business processes and systems in an organization. Essential functions include evaluating student work and assigning grades as well as meeting periodically with department supervisor to discuss class. Minimum Qualifications: An earned Masters degree or foreign equivalent in Information Systems or Business is required and closely related fields will be considered from an accredited university. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of demonstrated effectiveness in teaching at the university-level is preferred. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.  If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email Drake sheri.gavin@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. All 