    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Drake-University/Adjunct-Instructor--School-of-Law_JR100023": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nLaw School JM ‌ Department Summary: Drake Law School combines a rich history with the latest technology and an innovative curriculum, including the nation’s only First-Year Trial Practicum. As the only law school in the capital city of Des Moines, Drake Law School provides a unique educational and practical learning experience through modern facilities, a top-ranked legal clinic, and an exceptional relationship with the bench and bar. Drake Law School was founded in Des Moines in 1865, which makes it one of the 25 oldest law schools in the country. The Law School was established by Iowa Supreme Court justices George Wright and Chester Cole, who aimed to teach law in proximity to the courts so students could witness the law in action. From the very beginning, Drake Law School focused on real and practical experience. Today we continue to build on that tradition and provide opportunities for service, leadership, and the pursuit of rewarding careers. Learn more at: https://www.drake.edu/law/ Job Summary: Drake Law School seeks adjunct instructors to teach various areas of law.  Courses taught will vary from 1-4 hour credits. Minimum Qualifications: A J.D degree and experience teaching is required. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience preferred. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete online application and submit CV/resume and letter of interest. Review of applications will begin immediately. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Drake-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Law--Politics----Society_JR100022": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Law, Politics, & Society",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCollege of Arts and Sciences JM ‌ Department Summary: The Program in Law, Politics, and Society (LPS) at Drake University is a unique interdisciplinary undergraduate legal studies program. Faculty come from various disciplines but share a commitment to undergraduate teaching and scholarship in the field of Law and Society. Students enjoy small, discussion-based classes on topics ranging from constitutional law to crime and film. Many students go on to law school, but LPS graduates can be found in government, politics, advocacy, non-profits, and more. LPS is housed in the College of Arts & Sciences, the largest academic unit at Drake University. Students choose from a variety of majors, including several unique interdisciplinary programs. The student experience includes opportunities for community engagement, campus involvement, study abroad, and internships taken for course credit. Advanced students pursue their own research interest through independent study and senior capstone courses. Job Summary: The Department of Law, Politics, and Society seeks one to two adjunct instructors with ability to teach a relevant topical elective course in the Spring of 2026, and perhaps other courses in subsequent semesters. Classes will be taught in person. Minimum Qualifications: Successful candidates should have a PhD, JD, Masters, or equivalent advanced degree. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate students ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.   If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email will.garriot@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Facilities-Planning-and-Management/Assistant-Director--Facilities-Planning-and-Management_JR100020": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Facilities Planning and Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFacilities Planning and Management ‌ Department Summary: Drake University is currently seeking a new team member to join our Facilities Planning and Management department. We are looking for a capable, service-minded individual who takes pride in their work and enjoys being part of a collaborative team.   This position offers the opportunity to work alongside an outstanding group of dedicated professionals who help keep our campus operating efficiently, safely, and beautifully every day. If you are motivated by service, teamwork, and making a visible impact on the campus community, we encourage you to apply and become part of the Drake family. Job Summary: The Assistant Director serves as a key member of the FPM leadership team. This position provides strong management and leadership to one or more of the following areas: HVAC, buildings, custodial, and/or grounds. Reporting to the Executive Director, Facilities, Planning & Management, this position serves as an operational leader and acts in the Executive Director’s absence when designated. This position is expected to report to campus during emergencies. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree, bachelor’s degree preferred, Five (5) years of increasingly responsible professional experience in facilities, operations, or related discipline Three (3) years of direct supervisory or management experience, including responsibility for employee performance, work planning, coaching, and accountability. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively Proficiency in Microsoft Office programs including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Preferred Qualifications/Skills/Knowledge: Strong knowledge of building systems, deferred maintenance prioritization processes, construction, and/or regulatory compliance. Experience managing multiple priorities, responding to operational challenges, and delivering results in a customer service-oriented environment. Proven ability to foster a collaborative, inclusive, collegial, and consensus building relationship at all levels of the university based on competence, trust, and respect. Knowledge of design process for capital projects and understanding of contracts and insurance requirements. Demonstrated experience as a strategic thinker with proven planning and organization skills to effectively manage multiple projects of varying size and complexity, and the ability to modify or adjust priorities. Essential Functions: 30% Provide leadership and department management Directly oversee and manage one or more FPM departments by providing clear direction, establishing priorities, and aligning team efforts with departmental and institutional goals. Cultivate a positive, inclusive work environment where employees are empowered, supported, and equipped to perform at their highest potential. Engages in recruitment, hiring and training of FPM staff. Maintains and schedules monthly staff safety training, professional development planning processes and conducts employee performance reviews. Fosters a culture of safety. 20% Manage departmental planning and continuous improvement efforts Assist in the development and implementation of unit-level planning documents, including the FP&M continuous improvement plan and the facilities condition index. In close collaboration with all FPM managers, develop response plans to the administrative services survey (an internal customer service survey) and annual employee morale surveys. Develop and implement new ways to continually improve reporting, monitoring, and implementation of unit plans. 20% Lead communication efforts and build relationships Serve as a liaison between FPM and campus constituents by fostering effective communication regarding work orders, maintenance activities, construction projects, facility-related issues, and operational concerns. Coordinate with faculty, staff, students, and departmental representatives to provide timely updates, address questions, manage expectations, and ensure customer concerns are appropriately resolved. Monitor work orders to ensure timely communication with constituents and support employees in their respective communications efforts. Serve on university committees and ad hoc task forces, as assigned. 10% Provide budget oversight and monitoring Assist in the fiscal management of assigned FPM operations, including the development, administration, and monitoring of departmental operating and capital budgets. Analyze expenditures and revenue trends, prepare financial forecasts, reconcile accounts, and ensure resources are allocated effectively to support departmental priorities. 10% Manage safety and emergency management functions Oversee and ensure campus buildings have annual safety building inspections and are in full compliance with building codes and regulatory agencies. Work collaboratively with other campus partners on emergency management planning and as needed, play a key role in the deployment of emergency plans. Partners with Environmental Health & Safety and other stakeholders to identify, assess, and mitigate operational and compliance risks. 5% Oversee project management and issue resolution Provides management guidance and technical direction in the resolution of problems associated with maintenance, facilities and landscaping issues. Work with contractors to ensure the most appropriate course of action and to oversee the implementation of assigned repair or maintenance projects. Responds to emergencies and shutdowns, both during and outside regular shifts. 5% Performs other duties as assigned Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.  ‌ If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email kevin.moran@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Head-Start/Head-Start-Teacher--Southridge-10-months-_JR100021": {
      "title": "Head Start Teacher (Southridge-10 months)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHead Start Program Coordinator1 ‌ Department Summary: The Mission of Head Start and Early Head Start is a noble one: \"Better preparing young children and their families for now and in the future.\" Drake University Head Start and Early Head Start programs support the comprehensive development of children from birth to Age 5, in classroom settings, home-based programs, and child care partner locations. Job Summary: This position is responsible for leading children ages 3-5 and a teacher associate in daily classroom activities. The lead teacher is responsible for developing, implementing, and evaluating early childhood, developmentally appropriate curriculum and practice. Minimum Qualifications: B.S. or B.A. in Early Childhood Education or Elementary Education, or Early Childhood Special Education. One year of experience in a preschool environment. Ability to pass all state childcare licensing requirements. Ability to be insured by the University's insurance carrier. Preferred Qualifications: Early Childhood endorsement Current teaching license with special education endorsement. Head Start/Early Head Start experience. Current driver's license Essential Job Functions: 25% Maintain children's files, check off forms at admission, file them and check annually for licensing. Document and monitor children's progress to evaluate appropriateness of curriculum to meet children's developmental needs. Create and maintain accurate, confidential reports and records within applicable regulations and performance standards. 25% Conduct instruction by following lesson plan while adapting plan to meet individual learning styles. Create a developmentally appropriate environment where children are comfortable enough to verbalize feelings, question, explore, experiment and problem solve. Support children's social-emotional development. Promote successful classroom performance for each teaching team. 15% Develop and maintain good communication while respecting confidentiality. Establish rapport and trust with parents, staff, volunteers, and visitors to respond to children's environmental needs. Ensure the coordination of health issues of children and families with designated nurses. 15% Partner with staff in the development and implementation of the curriculum and maintaining a safe, orderly, and high-quality work environment. Ensure an organized, clean classroom and present interesting ideas and activities to share with children. 10% Partner with Teacher Associate to ensure classroom compliance with federal, state and local regulations of the Child & Adult Care Food Program (CACFP). Participate in mealtime activities by assisting with serving food, eating with the children, and cleaning up after meals. 5% Conduct initial and ongoing family home visits and socializations (if applicable). Travel for business purposes within service area. 5% Federal Head Start Program Performance Standards, state and local regulations, rules and requirements compliance. Maintain strict confidentiality of all records and documents. Maintain department records and reports in a secure manner. Continue professional growth by attending classes and workshops, reading new materials, and contributing resources to the program. Represent Drake University and Drake University Head Start in a professional manner. Treat clients, co-workers, staff, parents and community members with respect and civility, and ensure a safe and inclusive environment for everyone at all times. React to change productively, maintain prompt and regular attendance, and perform all other duties as assigned. Promote Head Start philosophy and initiatives. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.  If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email jackie.pafford@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Head-Start/Head-Start-Teacher--Wonder-Years-10-months-_JR100018": {
      "title": "Head Start Teacher (Wonder Years-10 months)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHead Start Program Coordinator2 ‌ Department Summary: The Mission of Head Start and Early Head Start is a noble one: \"Better preparing young children and their families for now and in the future.\" Drake University Head Start and Early Head Start programs support the comprehensive development of children from birth to Age 5, in classroom settings, home-based programs, and child care partner locations. Job Summary: This position is responsible for leading children ages 3-5 and a teacher associate in daily classroom activities. The lead teacher is responsible for developing, implementing, and evaluating early childhood, developmentally appropriate curriculum and practice. Minimum Qualifications: B.S. or B.A. in Early Childhood Education or Elementary Education, or Early Childhood Special Education. One year of experience in a preschool environment. Ability to pass all state childcare licensing requirements. Ability to be insured by the University's insurance carrier. Preferred Qualifications: Early Childhood endorsement Current teaching license with special education endorsement. Head Start/Early Head Start experience. Current driver's license Essential Job Functions: 25% Maintain children's files, check off forms at admission, file them and check annually for licensing. Document and monitor children's progress to evaluate appropriateness of curriculum to meet children's developmental needs. Create and maintain accurate, confidential reports and records within applicable regulations and performance standards. 25% Conduct instruction by following lesson plan while adapting plan to meet individual learning styles. Create a developmentally appropriate environment where children are comfortable enough to verbalize feelings, question, explore, experiment and problem solve. Support children's social-emotional development. Promote successful classroom performance for each teaching team. 15% Develop and maintain good communication while respecting confidentiality. Establish rapport and trust with parents, staff, volunteers, and visitors to respond to children's environmental needs. Ensure the coordination of health issues of children and families with designated nurses. 15% Partner with staff in the development and implementation of the curriculum and maintaining a safe, orderly, and high-quality work environment. Ensure an organized, clean classroom and present interesting ideas and activities to share with children. 10% Partner with Teacher Associate to ensure classroom compliance with federal, state and local regulations of the Child & Adult Care Food Program (CACFP). Participate in mealtime activities by assisting with serving food, eating with the children, and cleaning up after meals. 5% Conduct initial and ongoing family home visits and socializations (if applicable). Travel for business purposes within service area. 5% Federal Head Start Program Performance Standards, state and local regulations, rules and requirements compliance. Maintain strict confidentiality of all records and documents. Maintain department records and reports in a secure manner. Continue professional growth by attending classes and workshops, reading new materials, and contributing resources to the program. Represent Drake University and Drake University Head Start in a professional manner. Treat clients, co-workers, staff, parents and community members with respect and civility, and ensure a safe and inclusive environment for everyone at all times. React to change productively, maintain prompt and regular attendance, and perform all other duties as assigned. Promote Head Start philosophy and initiatives. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter.  If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email jackie.pafford@drake.edu A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. All offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
